@startuml
title CNC Motion Control - System Overview (lookahead branch, March 2026)
' Architecture: Single OCP1_ISR, Bresenham + velocity profiling inside ISR,
' look-ahead backward-pass planner, period-based TMR4/OC1/TMR5
!theme blueprint

participant "GCODE_Tasks\n(✅ Complete)" as GCODE
participant "UTILS_Module\n(✅ Complete)" as UTILS
participant "APP_Tasks\n(✅ Complete)" as APP
participant "KINEMATICS\n(✅ Lookahead)" as KINEMATICS
participant "STEPPER\n(✅ Complete)" as STEPPER
participant "MOTION_Tasks\n(✅ Complete)" as MOTION
participant "LIMIT_CHECK\n(✅ Complete)" as LIMITS
participant "TMR4\n(Period-Based\n781.25 kHz)" as TMR4
participant "OC1\n(Dual Compare)" as OC1HW
participant "OCP1_ISR\n(IPL5 Shadow Regs\nAll Axes)" as OC1ISR
participant "TMR5\n(One-Shot\nPulse Width)" as TMR5

== G-code Reception & Parsing ==
GCODE -> GCODE : Receive "G90G1X100Y25F1000S200M3"
GCODE -> UTILS : Call UTILS_TokenizeGcodeLine()
UTILS -> UTILS : Split: ["G90", "G1X100Y25F1000", "S200", "M3"]
UTILS -> GCODE : Return tokenized commands
GCODE -> GCODE : Store in gcodeCommandQueue (circular buffer, flow-controlled)

== Event-Driven Processing in APP_Tasks ==
APP -> GCODE : GCODE_GetNextEvent(&cmdQueue, &event)
GCODE -> APP : event (G1, G90, M3, etc.)

alt event.type == GCODE_EVENT_LINEAR_MOVE
    APP -> APP : Check soft limits
    APP -> KINEMATICS : KINEMATICS_PlanSegment(start, end, feedrate)
    KINEMATICS -> KINEMATICS : Bresenham deltas, dominant axis, abs_delta[]
    KINEMATICS -> KINEMATICS : Look-ahead backward pass:\n  - Junction velocity (cos angle)\n  - Trapezoidal accel/decel planning\n  - rate_delta, decel_rate_delta computed
    KINEMATICS -> APP : MotionSegment (fully planned)
    APP -> APP : Enqueue in motionQueue[16]
end

alt event.type == GCODE_EVENT_ARC_MOVE
    APP -> APP : Compute center, radius, angle, segment count
    APP -> APP : arcGenState = ARC_GEN_ACTIVE
    loop One segment per APP_Tasks() iteration
        APP -> KINEMATICS : KINEMATICS_PlanSegment() for arc chord
        KINEMATICS -> APP : MotionSegment
        APP -> APP : Enqueue in motionQueue[16]
    end
end

== Hard Limit Monitoring (Every APP_Tasks Iteration) ==
APP -> LIMITS : MOTION_UTILS_CheckHardLimits(invert_mask)
alt Hard limit triggered
    LIMITS -> APP : return true
    APP -> STEPPER : STEPPER_DisableAll()
    APP -> APP : APP_ALARM state, clear queues, send "ALARM:1"
end

== Segment Load (STEPPER_LoadSegment — main loop) ==
MOTION -> STEPPER : STEPPER_LoadSegment(segment)
STEPPER -> STEPPER : Populate ISR statics:\n  delta[], abs_delta[], dominant_axis,\n  dominant_delta, error[], direction_bits
STEPPER -> STEPPER : Set direction GPIO pins (Harmony macros)\n  DirX_Set/Clear, DirY_Set/Clear, etc.\n  DIR must be stable BEFORE first STEP rising edge
STEPPER -> TMR4 : PR4 = initial_rate (sets rollover period)
STEPPER -> OC1HW : OC1R = period - 5, OC1RS = period - 3
STEPPER -> TMR4 : TMR4_Start() / OCMP1_Enable() if not running
note right of STEPPER
  Segment transition race window:
  currentSegment assigned before ISR statics populated.
  One ISR fire may use prior-segment statics.
  Practically harmless — same pattern as GRBL.
end note

== Per-Step Cycle (OCP1_ISR — all axes, full Bresenham) ==
TMR4 -> OC1HW : Counts to OC1R → Step pin HIGH (rising edge)
TMR4 -> OC1HW : Counts to OC1RS → OCP1_ISR fires
activate OC1ISR
note over OC1ISR
  M14K Shadow Register Set (IPL5):
  Hardware register swap in 1 cycle.
  Zero push/pop stack cost on entry/exit.
end note
OC1ISR -> OC1ISR : Cache seg = currentSegment (NULL guard)
OC1ISR -> OC1ISR : Dominant axis STEP HIGH\n  switch(dominant_axis) → Harmony macro → LATxSET\n  Compiler: jump table → 1 branch + 1 register write
OC1ISR -> OC1ISR : AXIS_IncrementSteps / AXIS_DecrementSteps\n  (always_inline — address never taken → genuine inline)
OC1ISR -> OC1ISR : Bresenham loop (max 3 subordinate axes)\n  error[axis] += abs_delta[axis]\n  if error >= dominant_delta:\n    switch(axis) → StepY_Set()/StepZ_Set()/StepA_Set()\n    AXIS_IncrementSteps / DecrementSteps\n    error[axis] -= dominant_delta
OC1ISR -> TMR5 : T5CONSET = _T5CON_ON_MASK (direct SFR — start one-shot)
OC1ISR -> OC1ISR : Velocity profiling (integer only, no float, no division)\n  ACCEL: step_interval -= rate_delta  (precomputed look-ahead)\n  DECEL: step_interval += decel_rate_delta\n  CRUISE: unchanged
OC1ISR -> OC1ISR : Direct SFR: PR4 = period, OC1R = p-5, OC1RS = p-3
OC1ISR -> OC1ISR : seg->steps_completed++
deactivate OC1ISR
TMR4 -> TMR4 : Rolls over at PR4 → next cycle

== Pulse Width Expiry (~2.56 µs) ==
TMR5 -> OC1ISR : TMR5_PulseWidthCallback()
OC1ISR -> OC1ISR : T5CONCLR = _T5CON_ON_MASK (stop one-shot)
OC1ISR -> OC1ISR : StepX_Clear(); StepY_Clear(); StepZ_Clear(); StepA_Clear()\n  4 unrolled Harmony macros → 4 LATxCLR writes

== Segment Completion ==
MOTION -> MOTION : Poll steps_completed >= steps_remaining
MOTION -> MOTION : currentSegment = NULL, motionQueueCount--
MOTION -> MOTION : motionSegmentCompleted = true → deferred "ok" check
MOTION -> STEPPER : Load next segment from queue (seamless)

== Compile-Time Debug System ==
note over APP, MOTION
  Build: make BUILD_CONFIG=Debug DEBUG_FLAGS="DEBUG_MOTION DEBUG_STEPPER"
  Release: DEBUG_PRINT_XXX() macros compile to ((void)0) — zero bytes.
  Debug:   macros expand to UART_Printf() calls.
  No runtime checks, no if() overhead — pure preprocessor.
end note

== Build Commands ==
note over GCODE, LIMITS
  make                                         # Release build (default)
  make BUILD_CONFIG=Debug DEBUG_FLAGS="..."    # Debug build
  Always run from repository root directory.
end note

@enduml